# beehiiv-react — Windsurf Rules
# Read SKILL.md in the repo root for full conventions before making changes.

## Architecture summary
- src/client/   → Server-only BeehiivClient (API key lives here; never expose to client)
- src/hooks/    → Client-side React hooks that proxy through user-owned API routes
- src/components/ → BeehiivProvider context + SubscriptionForm drop-in component
- src/cli/      → Commander.js CLI (init + sync commands) with Handlebars code generators
- src/types/    → One file per resource; all re-exported through src/types/index.ts

## Hard rules
- BeehiivClient is server-only. Never import in hooks, components, or any client bundle.
- Hooks use useBeehiiv() for apiUrl. Never hardcode URLs.
- Hooks use fetchIdRef (useRef) to guard stale async responses.
- No any types. Strict TypeScript enforced via tsconfig.json.
- react and react-dom must stay as peerDependencies, never dependencies.
- Named exports everywhere except React components (default export allowed).
- chalk / ora / open are ESM-only — dynamic import() only, never top-level import.
- New types → src/types/index.ts + src/index.ts (both required).
- New features require tests. Baseline: 476 tests across 42 files.

## Feature addition order
Endpoint: types → types/index.ts → endpoint class → BeehiivClient → src/index.ts → tests
Hook:     src/hooks/use<Name>.ts → hooks/index.ts → src/index.ts → tests
Component: src/components/<Name>.tsx → components/index.ts → src/index.ts → tests

## CI (must pass before merge)
npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm test && npm run build
